[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-3430"] :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+8x-33 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =33 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2})-16 & =33 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16 & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square and solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}-16 & =33 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=49,$ and $p+q=53.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2} & =49 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4+7=3 \\\\ x & =-4-7=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-11$ and $x=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-30052"] :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+4 & =9 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2} & =5 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2})-4 & =5 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-4 & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}-4 & =5 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=-2,q=9,$ and $p+q=7.$\n\nNow, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-2)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2+3=5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2-3=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=5.$ Thus, the sum is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-112474"] :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+10t+13 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}+10t & =-13 \\\\ {t}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot t & =-13 \\\\ {t}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot t+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =-13 \\\\ (t+5)^{2}-25 & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t+5)^{2}-25 & =-13 \\\\ (t+5)^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=5,$ $q=12,$ and $p+q=17.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-112487/selection/e7246244c9d82c5699b691bf0636a1d30fe0c38416411d89130100da3fef8981" :answer/id #uuid "cef09595-ee12-5584-bfe1-6b1ea5c0d31b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=14,\\,m=-4\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112487/selection/4487146ec3ab1e0774cdd382ac7a45c0017a9088ac588299790df5a1dc3633ed" :answer/id #uuid "5a94e0c0-8946-54a2-989f-09d20106cc76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=10,\\,m=-2\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112487/selection/62c202b3a65b6b1213dfa29e02f710b8f3de6404410dbe0c32522080eba3fd3a" :answer/id #uuid "8dd374d6-e32d-5daf-8439-eb50db844239" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=8,\\,m=4\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112487/selection/a34dc0647f6c5b916945eeb71389d121b25ce36151b448e86946b57af94a41ef" :answer/id #uuid "1752d166-a3f3-517a-9092-c235d5186331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=10,\\,m=4\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112487/selection/2f89b8665c948dc845a42f91d9e3de9e2b53473cedbb79acbe45970828e39794" :answer/id #uuid "6c910fc9-faad-5356-be11-f0500ed12f51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=12,\\,m=-4\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112487/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab59f28a-c13f-5d55-837d-ebdb79eb165d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112487/selection/2f89b8665c948dc845a42f91d9e3de9e2b53473cedbb79acbe45970828e39794" :answer-field/choices ["q-112487/selection/e7246244c9d82c5699b691bf0636a1d30fe0c38416411d89130100da3fef8981" "q-112487/selection/4487146ec3ab1e0774cdd382ac7a45c0017a9088ac588299790df5a1dc3633ed" "q-112487/selection/62c202b3a65b6b1213dfa29e02f710b8f3de6404410dbe0c32522080eba3fd3a" "q-112487/selection/a34dc0647f6c5b916945eeb71389d121b25ce36151b448e86946b57af94a41ef" "q-112487/selection/2f89b8665c948dc845a42f91d9e3de9e2b53473cedbb79acbe45970828e39794"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112487" :question/id #uuid "6d70e8a4-cad6-5c6f-b225-88fe32f8d423" :question/math-academy-id "q-112487" :question/problem "The equation ${m}^{2}+8=-8m$ can be written in the form $(m+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $-8m$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+8 & =-8m \\\\ {m}^{2}+8m & =-8 \\\\ {m}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot m & =-8 \\\\ {m}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot m+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8 \\\\ (m+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8 \\\\ (m+4)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=8,$ and $p+q=12.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+4)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\sqrt{(m+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\ |m+4| & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\ m+4 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ m & =-4\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112490/selection/5d4d809199dba1fc0d6d3c21c466363322a784fda3af449c5eecb5d47c2be276" :answer/id #uuid "fdcabf79-d237-56bb-a9af-1eca5b811a8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=21,\\,a=3\\pm 5\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112490/selection/04f7f669540909bfac02f0b8d0d048333e6d7e099f185c6c1b60c3cb4cf3980d" :answer/id #uuid "a56e2508-b6cc-5d52-ae90-fba36150c1a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=24,\\,a=12\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112490/selection/eebbf8175fa0e31753d7e4f215d31ba52ee3fc5c8d1406f0cb13eacd96122ab5" :answer/id #uuid "75157e92-fcc3-56a4-818c-b86ac879ba58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=24,\\,a=6\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112490/selection/41b7b17ceacd669b2e8165b2b934ad842c1e603d28ef69d7a3020f68d6f56e57" :answer/id #uuid "838174d9-f82f-5f7d-854a-ce24092de414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=26,\\,a=2\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112490/selection/7c82c00570413bc33472f293047cfbd3c1a11b63961dbb7e7c1655abfd4d14a4" :answer/id #uuid "f54ca75a-0c67-5ef1-b9b9-6ccb51f93438" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=30,\\,a=1\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112490/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1476630-98ba-541a-adf5-49ce5fea2c87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112490/selection/eebbf8175fa0e31753d7e4f215d31ba52ee3fc5c8d1406f0cb13eacd96122ab5" :answer-field/choices ["q-112490/selection/5d4d809199dba1fc0d6d3c21c466363322a784fda3af449c5eecb5d47c2be276" "q-112490/selection/04f7f669540909bfac02f0b8d0d048333e6d7e099f185c6c1b60c3cb4cf3980d" "q-112490/selection/eebbf8175fa0e31753d7e4f215d31ba52ee3fc5c8d1406f0cb13eacd96122ab5" "q-112490/selection/41b7b17ceacd669b2e8165b2b934ad842c1e603d28ef69d7a3020f68d6f56e57" "q-112490/selection/7c82c00570413bc33472f293047cfbd3c1a11b63961dbb7e7c1655abfd4d14a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112490" :question/id #uuid "be8f497a-8c44-5854-8059-6756cc3a135d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112490" :question/problem "The equation ${a}^{2}-12a+18=0$ can be written in the form $(a-p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}-12a+18 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-12a & =-18 \\\\ {a}^{2}-2\\cdot 6\\cdot a+{6}^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-18 \\\\ (a-6)^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a-6)^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-18 \\\\ (a-6)^{2}-36 & =-18 \\\\ (a-6)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=6,q=18,$ and $p+q=24.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a-6)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\sqrt{(a-6)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\ |a-6| & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\ a-6 & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =6\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112490/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112490"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
